Contract: `Merge` copies all values from the input channels to one output channel and closes the output exactly once after every input channel is drained. The implementation is:

```go
func Merge(inputs ...<-chan int) <-chan int {
    out := make(chan int)
    var wg sync.WaitGroup

    for _, in := range inputs {
        wg.Add(1)
        go func(ch <-chan int) {
            defer wg.Done()
            defer close(out)
            for v := range ch {
                out <- v
            }
        }(in)
    }

    go func() {
        wg.Wait()
    }()
    return out
}
```

Does this meet the contract? If not, name the bug and give the minimal fix.
